{"assignees":[],"author":{"id":"U_kgDOEdWD9Q","is_bot":false,"login":"Markp1598M","name":""},"body":"## 📝 Description\nWhen using the Cobra library, registering a shell completion function for a persistent flag can cause a panic under certain conditions. Specifically, if a persistent flag is defined on a parent command and has a completion function registered, and a subcommand inherits this persistent flag, attempting to register a completion function for the same flag on the subcommand—or generating the shell completion scripts (Bash, Zsh, Fish, PowerShell) for the command tree—results in a runtime panic.\n\nThis panic typically occurs due to duplicate registration conflicts in the internal completion maps or nil pointer dereferences when traversing the command hierarchy to resolve flag completion functions.\n\n## 🎯 Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Registering a flag completion function via `RegisterFlagCompletionFunc` on a subcommand for an inherited persistent flag must not panic.\n- [ ] If a subcommand registers its own completion function for an inherited persistent flag, it should cleanly override the parent command's completion function for that subcommand and its children, without affecting the parent command's completion behavior.\n- [ ] Shell completion generation functions (e.g., `GenBashCompletionV2`, `GenZshCompletion`, `GenFishCompletion`, `GenPowerShellCompletion`) must execute successfully without panicking when the command tree contains inherited persistent flags with registered completion functions.\n- [ ] Comprehensive unit tests must be added to verify duplicate registration safety and correct resolution order (subcommand override vs. parent default).\n\n## 🛠️ Technical Specifications & Context\nIn `cobra`, flag completions are managed via the `Command` struct and its associated completion registration methods.\n\n### Key Files:\n- `command.go`: Contains `RegisterFlagCompletionFunc` and the command structure.\n- `shell_completions.go`: Contains the logic for resolving and executing completion functions during shell interaction.\n- `bash_v2.go`, `zsh.go`, `fish.go`, `powershell.go`: Script generation files that traverse the command tree and inspect flag completion functions.\n\n### Proposed Implementation Details:\n1. **Safe Registration in `command.go`**:\n   In `Command.RegisterFlagCompletionFunc(flagName string, f func(*Command, []string, string) ([]string, ShellCompDirective))`:\n   - Ensure the internal map `cmd.flagCompletionFuncs` is safely initialized.\n   - If the flag is an inherited persistent flag, allow the subcommand to register its own completion function in its local `flagCompletionFuncs` map. This should act as a local override.\n\n2. **Resolution Logic in `shell_completions.go`**:\n   When resolving a completion function for a flag:\n   - The resolution logic should traverse upwards from the target subcommand to the parent commands.\n   - It should return the first completion function found for the flag, starting from the subcommand where the execution was triggered. This ensures overrides are respected.\n   - Prevent duplicate registration panics in the shell script generators by ensuring they do not attempt to register the same flag completion key multiple times in global script scopes.\n\n## 🧪 Verification & Testing\n\n### Reproduction Test Case\nAdd a test case in `command_test.go` or `shell_completions_test.go` similar to the following:\n\n```go\nfunc TestSubcommandPersistentFlagCompletionNoPanic(t *testing.T) {\n    rootCmd := &Command{Use: \"root\"}\n    subCmd := &Command{Use: \"sub\"}\n    \n    rootCmd.PersistentFlags().String(\"config\", \"\", \"config file\")\n    rootCmd.AddCommand(subCmd)\n    \n    // Register on parent\n    err := rootCmd.RegisterFlagCompletionFunc(\"config\", func(cmd *Command, args []string, toComplete string) ([]string, ShellCompDirective) {\n        return []string{\"xml\", \"json\"}, ShellCompDirectiveDefault\n    })\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"Failed to register completion on root: %v\", err)\n    }\n    \n    // Register override on subcommand (should not panic)\n    defer func() {\n        if r := recover(); r != nil {\n            t.Errorf(\"Registration on subcommand panicked: %v\", r)\n        }\n    }()\n    \n    err = subCmd.RegisterFlagCompletionFunc(\"config\", func(cmd *Command, args []string, toComplete string) ([]string, ShellCompDirective) {\n        return []string{\"yaml\", \"toml\"}, ShellCompDirectiveDefault\n    })\n    if err != nil {\n        t.Fatalf(\"Failed to register completion override on subcommand: %v\", err)\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Running Tests\nVerify the fix by running the package tests:\n```bash\ngo test -v ./...\n```\n\n---\n\n[![Opire Bounty](https://img.shields.io/badge/bounty-Opire-emerald?style=for-the-badge)](https://github.com/Markp1598M/cobra)\n<br/>\n<hr/>\n\n<details><summary>This repo is using Opire - what does it mean? 👇</summary><br/>💵 Everyone can add rewards for this issue commenting <code>/reward 100</code> (replace <code>100</code> with the amount).<br/>🕵️‍♂️ If someone starts working on this issue to earn the rewards, they can comment <code>/try</code> to let everyone know!<br/>🙌 And when they open the PR, they can comment <code>/claim #1</code> either in the PR description or in a PR's comment.<br/><br/>🪙 Also, everyone can tip any user commenting <code>/tip 20 @Markp1598M</code> (replace <code>20</code> with the amount, and <code>@Markp1598M</code> with the user to tip).<br/><br/>📖 If you want to learn more, check out our <a href=\"https://docs.opire.dev\">documentation</a>.</details>","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOTMIJhc8AAAABImU1Lw","author":{"login":"Markp1598M"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"/reward 10","createdAt":"2026-07-03T02:20:10Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/Markp1598M/cobra/issues/1#issuecomment-4872025391","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOTMIJhc8AAA